# Django timestamps

Concrete Django models in this project inherit `TimeStampedModel` for ORM-managed `created_at` / `updated_at`.

## Do

- Subclass `TimeStampedModel` (from `news.models` or the app’s shared base) for new concrete models
- Rely on the base fields; do not re-declare `created_at` / `updated_at`
- When using `save(update_fields=[...])`, include `"updated_at"` if the bump should apply

## Don't

- Skip timestamps on app-owned concrete models without a reason
- Re-declare duplicate timestamp fields by hand
- Apply this to Django built-in apps or unmanaged models

## Exception

Omit `TimeStampedModel` only with a one-line comment explaining why (e.g. unmanaged / read-only proxy).
